            <ArticleTitle>An incidental talonavicular coalition in a diabetic patient: a podiatric perspective.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/bcr-2014-204510</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">bcr2014204510</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A tarsal coalition is a pathological union of two or more tarsal bones. The authors present an incidental finding of a unilateral talonavicular (TN) coalition that was overlooked in a 57-year-old diabetic female with signs and symptoms of peripheral neuropathy. This case highlights the clinical implications and important teaching points in recognising a TN coalition. This is particularly relevant for new, upcoming clinicians who may have never been exposed to this diagnostic rarity during clinical training.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>2014 BMJ Publishing Group Ltd.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
